# Exudyn .gitattributes
#
# Line endings: text files are stored LF in the repository and checked out in the platform's
# native form. All generation and building has happened on Windows so far, so this is what keeps
# a generator run on Linux from producing whole-file diffs (revision2026 step R0.5, fact 18).
#
# The index was already fully LF-normalised when this file was added (2003 text files), so it
# introduced no renormalisation. If that ever changes, `git add --renormalize .` fixes it in one
# reviewable commit.
#
# WARNING: do not add a blanket `*.rst text` rule.
# main/pythonDev/TestModels/testData/rotorAnsys.rst is an ANSYS *result* file, not
# reStructuredText — binary, with several hundred thousand NUL bytes. It is marked below.

* text=auto

#+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
# Explicit end-of-line requirements
#+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
# shell scripts must be LF or they fail under sh/bash, including in WSL and docker
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Windows batch files: CRLF avoids trouble with labels and goto on some shells
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Visual Studio writes and expects CRLF; VS2022 is the primary development environment
*.sln           text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj       text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj.*     text eol=crlf
*.pyproj        text eol=crlf

#+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
# Binary — never convert, never diff as text
#+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
# ANSYS result files; note the .rst extension clash with reStructuredText
main/pythonDev/TestModels/testData/*.rst    binary

# images
# NOTE: *.eps and *.stl are deliberately NOT listed. Both have ASCII variants —
# docs/theDoc/figures/triangleNormal.eps is plain PostScript with no NUL bytes, and forcing
# it binary would store its CRLFs and show a spurious 1197-byte change. text=auto detects
# the binary variants (DOS-preview EPS, binary STL) correctly by their NUL bytes.
*.png           binary
*.PNG           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.bmp           binary
*.ico           binary
*.cdr           binary

# documents and media
*.pdf           binary
*.mp4           binary
*.avi           binary
*.mov           binary

# numerical and mesh data
*.npy           binary
*.npz           binary
*.pkl           binary
*.h5            binary
*.hdf5          binary
*.slx           binary

# compiled artefacts
*.lib           binary
*.a             binary
*.dll           binary
*.dylib         binary
*.so            binary
*.pyd           binary
*.pdb           binary
*.obj           binary
*.exe           binary
*.zip           binary
*.whl           binary

# fonts
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
